From 7f88530fed5698e98a4e55aec360d656e126c765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:54:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 093/119] fix: the ODT field's default lived only in the
 reflection, so an untouched camera loaded no output transform

Root cause: SCineOutputParams::odtFile had no in-class initialiser. The
Schematyc::CSharedString("Assets/ODT/odt_srgb_100nit_aces2_65.cube") passed to
AddMember feeds the REFLECTED default - graph node defaults, "reset to default",
the serializer's skip-if-equal test - and never assigns the member. So the value
the runtime read at activation was an empty string, EnsureLutSlot took the
"empty path is a legitimate answer" branch meant for the LMT slot, cleared the
ODT slot without a word, and the tone map fell through to D13's clamped encode:
the flat, washed picture the first runtime test reported. Typing any path in
worked because that went through the property-changed path with a non-empty
string; the ICryPak lookup itself was never at fault.

Three changes:

- The member gets the in-class initialiser it was missing, from a new
  kDefaultODTFile constant that is now the single definition of the shipped
  default (member initialiser, reflected default, and the fallback below).
- ApplyDisplayLuts substitutes kDefaultODTFile for an empty field. Levels saved
  before this commit have an empty string ON DISK, so the initialiser alone
  would not repair them; and an unset field is not a statement about the
  display, it is a field nobody has touched.
- The load is now diagnosable. Success logs the ABSOLUTE path the cube came from
  (ICryPak::AdjustFileName), because "not found" and "found in the other install
  tree" are indistinguishable in a relative path and those two trees are exactly
  the pair that gets confused. Failure is a CryWarning, not a CryLog, and names
  both absolute paths that were tried - D13's behaviour is kept, but the reason
  is no longer something the user has to go looking for.

README.md and docs/SceneReferredLook.md updated for the empty-field rule and the
new log lines.

